<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Proposal 45 M3, AC3.3 / D4b: the ring goes THROUGH the master lane's chain: 2 x 0.082071 = 0.164142. Under the linear split it would read 0.082071, and that is the whole difference between the two modes.

  ONE MEASUREMENT PER CASE, AND THAT IS NOT STYLE. The playback capture is
  CUMULATIVE across phases in one process - arming, playing, stopping and
  disarming does not restart the device, so the recording grows (measured:
  256000, 535552, 815104, 1094656 frames over four phases) and a fixed window
  reads the FIRST phase every time. A four-phase version of this gate returned
  the identical 0.100520 four times over and would have passed while measuring
  nothing. The four cases below therefore share a fixture and a window and
  differ in one setting each.

  THE FOUR RELATED CASES, whose bands are DISJOINT by construction - that is
  what makes them a discriminator rather than four sanity checks:

    master_closure_linear_ring            ring alone, no master   0.082071
    master_closure_heard_ring             ring alone, 2.0x master 0.164142
    master_closure_heard_root             + root at -12 dB        0.201010
    master_closure_heard_root_raised      + root at  -6 dB        0.283790

  Rows 1 vs 2 are the mode itself: under the LINEAR split the ring bypasses the
  master, under CLOSURE it goes through it. Same fixture, same window, one
  master insert apart. Rows 3 vs 4 are the ROOT-PRESENCE
  discriminator - raising the unarmed track 6 dB must move the level by
  1.4118. Before AC3.1 was rebuilt to suppress the frozen SUM rather than the
  frozen PULL, the same change moved it by 1.0046: the arrangement was absent,
  because twSpeaker publishes the transport position from
  engine->currentPosition() AFTER the pull it had stopped making, so the
  playhead never advanced.

  THE MEASUREMENT WINDOW IS THE HARD PART, and a first attempt got it wrong in
  both directions. TOO EARLY sits inside the monitor priming lag (twSpeaker
  defers the device start until the readahead is primed) and read BIMODALLY -
  0.23158 four times and 0.461913 once, same binary, same script. TOO LATE
  runs past the end of the material, halves one source, and reads exactly like
  the other source alone; that artifact was very nearly written up as an
  engine defect. Hence: the fixture is placed TWICE for 8 s and the window is
  [168000, 216000) - 3.5 to 4.5 s.

  THE SOURCES ARE UNCORRELATED ON PURPOSE: the root carries test_autosaw.wav
  and the ring test_sawtooth.wav, so their sum is sqrt of the sum of squares
  regardless of a relative phase nothing here controls. Two copies of one
  signal have no closed-form sum, and every band would have to widen until it
  separated nothing.

  HEADROOM IS PART OF THE MEASUREMENT, NOT HOUSEKEEPING. The armed track runs
  through a 0.25 gain so the 2.0x master does not clip. An earlier probe put
  that master over full-scale sources, clipped the 16-bit capture at peak
  exactly 1.0000, and read as an unexplained ~11 % shortfall.
-->
<SActionScript version="1" name="master_closure_heard_ring">

  <setup project="new"/>

  <actions>
    <!-- Track 0: armed and monitored, on the paced file input carrying
         test_sawtooth.wav (RMS 0.328284), through a 0.25 gain = 0.082071. -->
    <add-track index="-1"/>
    <set-track-input trackPath="0" input="audio:file:3"/>
    <set-monitor-mode trackPath="0" mode="on"/>
    <insert-plugin trackPath="0" slotIndex="0"
                   format="clap" uid="tw.test.clap.gain"
                   name="Smaragd Test Gain" vendor="Smaragd"
                   path="twtestclap.clap" nIn="2" nOut="2"/>
    <set-plugin-param trackPath="0" slotIndex="0" paramId="0" value="0.25"/>

    <!-- Track 1: NEVER armed. test_autosaw.wav (RMS 0.230956) placed twice for
         8 s of material. -->
    <add-track index="-1"/>
    <add-sample trackPath="1" filePath="../test_autosaw.wav" timePos="0"/>
    <add-sample trackPath="1" filePath="../test_autosaw.wav" timePos="192000"/>
    <set-track-volume trackPath="1" volume="-60"/>
    <insert-plugin trackPath="$master" slotIndex="0"
                   format="clap" uid="tw.test.clap.gain"
                   name="Smaragd Test Gain" vendor="Smaragd"
                   path="twtestclap.clap" nIn="2" nOut="2"/>
    <set-plugin-param trackPath="$master" slotIndex="0" paramId="0" value="2.0"/>
    <arm-track trackPath="0" armed="1"/>
    <set-locator position="0"/>
    <toggle-playback play="1"/>
    <wait-playhead minAdvance="4096" timeoutMs="30000"/>
    <wait-ms ms="5200"/>
    <toggle-playback play="0"/>
    <dump-playback-capture filename="master_closure_heard_ring.wav" minFrames="216000"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="master_closure_heard_ring.wav" startFrame="168000" frameCount="48000"
                         channel="0" minRms="0.1592" maxRms="0.1691"/>
    <arm-track trackPath="0" armed="0"/>

    <!-- AC3.4: nobody rendered where they were not allowed to. Under Closure
         the pump runs the master lane's OWN processor instances, so a freeze
         worker touching one of them is exactly the two-thread hazard D4b
         names. -->
    <assert-render-policy liveThreadRefusals="0" liveOwnedRefusals="0"/>
  </actions>

  <assertions>
    <assert-track-count equals="2"/>
  </assertions>

</SActionScript>
